$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (+)-9 from (−)-12 (Scheme 2) To a solution of (−)-12 (1.20
g, 4.79 mmol) and NaHCO3 (4.03 g, 47.9 mmol) in trifluoroacetone-H2O
(1:1, 12 mL) at -15 °C, was added Oxone® every 15 min (4 x 1.50 g, 4 x
2.4 mmol) with stirring. After 3 h, TBME (30 mL) was added in the
reaction mixture and filtered with celite. The filtrate was treated with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (20 mL) and extracted with TBME (3 x 20 mL). The
combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and the solvent
was removed under reduced pressure to afford a crude residue, which was
purified by column chromatography (eluent: hexane: EtOAc = 5: 1). (+)-9
(0.92 g, 72%) as a colorless oil. [α]D 25 +24.7 (c 0.68, CHCl3); IR
(liquid film) νmax 1722 (C=O), 1654 (C=C) cm-1; 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz,
ppm) δ 1.34−1.70 (10H, m), 3.68 (1H, dd, J = 3.6, 2.4 Hz, H-5), 3.84 (3H,
s, COOMe), 3.99 (1H, ddd, J = 3.8, 1.7, 0.6 Hz, H-6), 4.57 (1H, dd, J =
6.8, 2.4 Hz, H-3), 4.80 (1H, br d, J = 6.8 Hz, H-4), 6.83 (1H, m, H-2);
13C-NMR (CDCl3, 150 MHz, ppm) δ 23.7, 23.9, 24.8, 35.2, 37.4, 46.1, 49.3,
52.3, 70.0, 70.8, 111.6, 127.1, 140.3, 165.5 ; HRMS m/z calcd for
C14H18O5 (M)+ 266.1156, found 266.1161.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, oxone was added every 15 minutes over 3
hours, key intermediate
