$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1,2-epoxyheptane (251). To a solution of 1-heptene (286,
1.00 g, 10.2 mmol, 1.0 eq.) in CH2Cl2 (50 mL) was added mCPBA (2.09 g,
12.2 mmol, 1.2 eq.). After 3 h stirring at room temperature the mixture
was quenched by the addition of saturated NaHCO3 (30 mL), followed by the
extraction with CH2Cl2 (3x 50 mL). The combined organic layers were
washed with NaOH (2 M, 25 mL), dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. Column chromatography on silica gel with
pentane/diethyl ether (10:1) yielded 251 Colourless liquid, yield (765
mg, 7.24 mmol, 72%). UV (CH2Cl2) λmax (log ε) 237 (2.28) nm; IR
(diamond): νmax 2958, 2929, 2860, 915, 829, 732 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 2.91 (1H, ddt, J = 4.0, 2.8, 5.5 Hz, 1x CH), 2.75 (1H, dd, J =
4.0, 5.7 Hz, CH2), 2.47 (1H, dd, J = 2.7, 5.1 Hz, CH2), 1.56-1.40 (4H, m,
2x CH2), 1.40-1.28 (4H, m, 2x CH2), 0.83 (3H, t, J = 7.2 Hz, CH3); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CHCl3) δ 52.4 (CH), 47.1 (CH2), 32.5 (CH2), 31.6 (CH2),
25.6 (CH2), 22.6 (CH2), 14.0 (CH3); EIMS m/z 114 [M]+ (<1), 99 (4), 81
(10), 71 (96), 56 (78), 41 (100); GC (BPX-5) I = 912; GC (HP-5MS) I =
959.
