$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 2 (GP 2): Epoxidation of
Olefins by m-CPBA: The olefin (2.00 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (20
mL). At 0 °C m-CPBA (518 mg, 3.00 mmol) was added. The mixture was
stirred at room temperature for the indicated time. After adding of Et2O
(50 mL) the mixture was washed with 2N NaOH (2x10 mL), the combined
aqueous layers were extracted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL). The combined organic
layers were washed with brine (5 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvents were
removed under reduced pressure and the crude product purified by SiO2
chromatography. 4-(2-Methyl-oxiranyl)-but-2-enoic acid
1,1,2,2-tetramethyl-propyl ester (24) According to GP 2 S6 (448 mg, 2.00
mmol) and m-CPBA (670 mg (77%), 3.00 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (30 ml) for 3 h.
SiO2 chromatography (PE:Et2O 95:5) gave 24 (341 mg, 71 %). Rf=0.2 (CH:EE
95:5). 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6): δ= 6.8 (ddd, 3 J H-H=15.6 Hz, 7.6 Hz, 7.1
Hz, 1H), 5.67 (ddd, 3 J H-H=15.6 Hz, 4 J H-H=1.5 Hz, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 2.16
(dq, 2 J H-H=4.8 Hz, 4 J H-H=0.7 Hz, 1H), 2.06 (dd, 2 J H-H=4.5 Hz, 4 J
H-H=0.6 Hz, 1H), 2.04 (dddd, 2 J H-H=14.7 Hz, 3 J H-H=7.6 Hz, 4 J H-H=1.3
Hz, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 1.96 (ddd, 2 J H-H=14.7 Hz, 3 J H-H=7.1 Hz, 4 J H-H=1.6
Hz, 1H), 1.53 (s, 6H), 0.96 (d, 4 J H-H=0.8 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (s, 9H). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, C6D6): δ= 165.2, 142.0, 86.6, 55.2, 52.3, 39.3, 38.5, 25.2,
21.0, 20.6 ppm. IR (film): ν=2980, 1715, 1655, 1465, 1380, 1265, 1170,
1130, 980, 850, 770 cm-1. HRMS: (EI, 70 eV): m/z calcd. for C13H21O3
225.1491; found 225.1492 [M-CH3 ]+.
