$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Catalytic Olefin Epoxidations by Cobalt
Catalyst with MCPBA. To a mixture of substrate (0.035 mmol), cobalt
catalyst (0.001 mmol), and solvent (CH3CN, 1 mL) was added MCPBA (0.05
mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 min at room temperature, even
though the reaction was complete within 1 min at room temperature (Figure
S1). Reaction was monitored by GC/mass analysis of 20 μL aliquots
withdrawn periodically from the reaction mixture. All reactions were run
at least three times, and the average product yields are presented.
Product yields were based on substrate. In a competitive reaction of
cis-2-octene and trans-2-octene, the concentration of the substrate was
0.20 mmol, respectively. Yield (93.6 ± 2.7%); 2-cyclohexen-1-ol: Yield
(1.1 ± 0.1%); 2-cyclohexenone: Yield (1.4 ± 0.1%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 96% conversion, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Terminal and Internal Olefin Epoxidation with Cobalt(II) as the Catalyst:
Evidence for an Active Oxidant CoII-Acylperoxo Species
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hyun, Min Young; Kim, Soo Hyun; Song, Young Joo; Lee, Hong Gyu; Jo, Young
Dan; Kim, Jin Hoon; Hwang, In Hong; Noh, Jin Young; Kang, Juhye; Kim,
Cheal
