$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical experimental procedure for the
epoxidation reactions described in Table 1, Table 3 and Scheme 10: The
reaction was carried out in a flat bottomed glass vial (diameter 15mm)
equipped with a magnetic stirrer flea. In the vial, were placed the amine
1 or the hydrochloride salt of amine 1, 2, 3, 7 or 8 (5 or 10 mol %,
0.0212 or 0.042 mmol), and 1-phenylcyclohexene (67 mg, 0.424 mmol). The
mixture was dissolved in CH3CN/H2O (0.5 mL) and pyridine (0.5 eq., 0.212
mmol, 17 μL) was added followed by finely ground NaHCO3 (356 mg, 4.24
mmol) and Oxone® (521 mg, 0.848 mmol). The reaction was stirred at room
temperature or at -10°C and followed by TLC. If the reaction was not
complete, stirring was continued for a maximum of 2 hours. Salts were
removed by filtration with a sinter over MgSO4. The cake was washed with
CH2Cl2 (25 mL). When the reaction was performed at -10°C (Table 1,
entries 4, 7 and 9), the organic phase was extracted with a saturated
solution of NaHCO3 (to recover the amine). After evaporation of the dried
organic phase, the crude mixture was analyzed by 1H NMR. Yields and
conversions are determined by 1H NMR relative to an internal standard
(para-dimethoxybenzene). The enantioselectivities were determined by
chiral GC using a α-CD column. Procedure for reaction described in Scheme
5: The reaction has been performed following the procedure described
above for Table 1 with CD3CN/D2O. After 5 min. of stirring at room
temperature, the reaction mixture was diluted with CDCl3 (2 mL) in the
presence of an internal standard. After 5 min. of stirring, the salts
were allowed to settle. Solvent was decanted for NMR analysis. Yields are
determined by 1H NMR relative to an internal standard
(para-dimethoxybenzene). (S,S)-1-phenylcyclohexene oxide, yield 38%;
potassium sulfate 6a, yield 90% 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 25 °C): =
1.20-1.71 (m, 4H; CH2), 1.92-2.38 (m, 4H; CH2), 3.01 (m, 1H; CHO),
7.21-7.53 (m, 5H; aromatic H). The absolute configuration was determined
by comparing the measured optical rotation with the reported one: [α]D20
= -54.8 (c = 0.47 in toluene) [lit.[5] for the
(R,R)-1-phenylcyclohex-1-ene oxide: [α]D25 = +116.7 (c = 1.21 in benzene)
for 98% ee].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
